INT. DEFUNCT ICE RINK, "SYNERGY KICKOFF" - DAY

A chilly arena with dead floodlights and a Zamboni parked in the corner like a retired elephant. Folding chairs in a semicircle. A banner: "WE ARE ONE TEAM." A podium with a microphone that squeals.

Six people sit with lukewarm coffee and laminated agendas. On the ice-less floor, where the center circle once glowed, a flip chart waits on a tripod.

                    COLM
          Okay, welcome everybody. Can everyone hear me?

                    ANNELIESE
          Yes.

                    COLM
          Great. Anneliese, you can hear me?

                    ANNELIESE
          I said yes.

                    DORCAS
          We could hear you in the car park.

                    COLM
          Wonderful. So today's theme is...

                    VIKRAM
          Alignment.

                    COLM
          Alignment, exactly, Vikram, thank you for that.

                    VIKRAM
          It's on the banner. Well, "one team" is. Alignment is on the agenda.

                    PENROSE
          I thought today's theme was resilience.

                    COLM
          It's both.

                    PENROSE
          They're different words.

                    COLM
          They're complementary words.

                    YUSRA
          Can I ask something?

                    COLM
          Of course, Yusra, we love questions.

                    YUSRA
          Why are we here? In the rink?

                    COLM
          It's a neutral space.

                    DORCAS
          It's a cold space.

                    COLM
          It builds character.

                    ANNELIESE
          My feet have no character left.

                    PENROSE
          I read the invitation twice. It said "off-site."

                    COLM
          It is off-site.

                    VIKRAM
          From what?

                    COLM
          From our usual site.

                    YUSRA
          Which is across the street.

                    COLM
          Which is a bit literal, Yusra.

                    YUSRA
          I'm literal on Mondays.

                    DORCAS
          It's Friday.

                    YUSRA
          I'm literal in general.

                    COLM
          Okay, let's move to the first exercise.

                    ANNELIESE
          Is there a second exercise?

                    COLM
          There are four.

                    PENROSE
          I have a flight.

                    COLM
          Penrose, your flight is at eight.

                    PENROSE
          This morning.

                    COLM
          No, tonight.

                    PENROSE
          It says eight a.m. on the ticket.

                    COLM
          I'm sure you misread it.

                    PENROSE
          I'm sure I didn't.

                    VIKRAM
          Could we maybe start with a break?

                    DORCAS
          We've only just started.

                    VIKRAM
          That's why we need a break.

                    COLM
          Let's table that.

                    ANNELIESE
          Where? There's no table.

                    YUSRA
          Colm, I think the Zamboni is leaking.

                    COLM
          It's a feature.

                    PENROSE
          It's a hazard.

                    COLM
          Everything's a hazard if you look at it right.

                    DORCAS
          Then maybe don't make us look.

                    COLM
          Dorcas.

                    DORCAS
          I'm only saying.

                    ANNELIESE
          Colm, can we have a vote?

                    COLM
          On what?

                    ANNELIESE
          On whether to leave.

                    COLM
          That's not on the agenda.

                    VIKRAM
          Neither is the cold.

                    YUSRA
          I vote leave.

                    PENROSE
          Leave.

                    DORCAS
          Leave.

                    VIKRAM
          Leave.

                    ANNELIESE
          Leave, obviously.

                    COLM
          Okay. Okay. Show of hands for staying?

                    COLM (CONT'D)
          Just me, then.

                    DORCAS
          We'll tell them you were wonderful.
